A||||14||frontal lobe||so that's it||||1||
Z||000000||frontal lobe||05-06-2000||12:56 AM||||Took my wife out on a date tonight and asked her if she wanted to take the Fiero, which she has only ridden in once in the 3 months I've had it.  She said no.  I asked why not.  She said I don't like the smell!<P>I agree with her that it does have that 13 year old interior musty-like smell.  Not bad, just typical.  <P>What do you guys use to make your interiors smell good?  (Please, no pine.  Also, no heavy perfume scents).  I need you guys to come through for me with some good advice or I may never get her in that car.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Eric||05-06-2000||01:15 AM||||Just bite the bullet and shampoo the carpet and seats.  Better yet, put in a new headliner with that funky smelling glue, and you'll have the fumes to choke her out or atleast give her a little buzz.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||05-06-2000||05:35 AM||||After steam cleaning/shampooing try my favorite air freshener. It's made by Glade and it's not a cover up. It's called "Neutralizer" and has it's own VERY pleasant odor. I took out all the vents and faceplates by unfastening the torx screws and stuck in about 5 of these in the round twist form and stuck'em on. On a damp day I just turn on the heat through the vent and get an extra blast! <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 05-06-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||Phil||05-06-2000||07:09 AM||||Shampoo as advised and then replace your seats with leather. Problem solved.||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||05-06-2000||07:56 AM||||i use Static Guard in my Jeep!  I have a terible problem with static from the seats, so i spray the thing down with static gaurd ever 2 weeks... keeps it kinda new smelling.  all my friends have commented that the jeep maintains a new odor.<P>but whatever you do, deffinately shampoo the inside as best you can, 1st.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||05-06-2000||11:30 AM||||fabreeze... take the carpet out of the car hose it down hang it over the fence for a day to dry,  fabreeze it and stick it back in the car.. thats what I did.. doesn't smell like ANYTHING now... the car is down for the weekend but not smelly and odd like it was on friday after work sitting in traffic with no A/C and diesel blowing into your face...   sorry...   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||05-06-2000||11:33 AM||||I totaly agree with 1fst2m6! Frabreeze did the job for my car. Try it, its only 4bucks.<BR>----Knight----||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||05-06-2000||12:32 PM||||Have you seen those air fresheners in a can? Looks sorta like sterno? Well the guy I bought my car from had one behind each seat. These things are so stinkin strong that even 2 years after I took them out, if I let my car sit for a while (couple of weeks), it smells like cherry certs when I get in. Thats some strong shtuff!||||reg||1
Z||000008||RobertVol||05-07-2000||03:20 AM||||Another Vote for Frebreeze!!! <P>takes that musty smell out easily.  ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phaeton||05-07-2000||04:29 AM||||If this is applicable.<P>Bacteria in the AC system ductwork.  The dealer sells a kit (not cheap) to kill the stubborn little rascals.<P>The older the car the more places stink has had time to hide in.  Do all the above and don't be afraid to cut and fit new insulation under the carpet (which was taken out for thorough cleaning), a nesting ground for elusive odors.||||reg||12
Z||000010||Sillhouette.com||05-07-2000||08:02 AM||||The posts all have good information.  Make sure you take your evaporator and heater core area appart.  Use Lysol on those areas to kill the bacteria and clean out all the leafs that gather there.  Also clean out all the leafs from under your front hood.  That is where the air enters your vehicle.   A good shampoo of your carper seats and headliner, use spraynine on the plastic trim and scrub followed by armorall.  Use fabreeze on the carpet for that smell.  If you got those removable carpets throw it away and buy new ones.  Hope this helps. <P><BR>Later.||||reg||1
Z||000011||frontal lobe||05-08-2000||11:13 PM||||Thanks a lot, guys.  Will try the shampooing and frebreeze (spelling?? it got spelled 3 different ways in the posts, I'll figure it out at the store).  <P>Stimpy, that is EXACTLY the kind of smell I was NOT looking for! If I put those in, I'd NEVER get Mrs. Sensitive Nose in the car!||||reg||1
Z||000012||stimpy||05-09-2000||07:18 AM||||I'm tellin ya! I can't see how that guy could stand it! I'd almost prefer catpiss smell to that strong of chemical. Phew!||||reg||1
Z||000013||theogre||05-09-2000||09:29 AM||||Fabreze and such work well but make sure you have plenty of moving air when you use it. Some of those products are very irratating if you breath it when you use them. Once they dry they are fine, just avoid breathing the mist durring use.<P>When the AC is shut off it's a perfect mold garden. Dark and warm and wet. The mold grows real quick and stinks wonderfully. That chemical AC cleaner is extreamly toxic, and is only temporary. It will wear off in a couple weeks. maybe longer depending on the system and usage. Then you're right back where you started.<P>I believe it's Chrysler that actually developed something better than the chemical AC cleaner. It is available as a unversal kit as well as an add on to thier cars that don't have it. I don't think it is very expensive. (No, I don't remember all the details.)<P>The device is esentially an small timer. When you shut off the car with the AC on it keeps the heater blower running for 10-15 minutes to dry out the AC system. That way there's not enough moisture to grow the molds that stink up the system.<P>You can get allot of the result of this device by getting into the habbit of switching from AC to Vent the last couple miles before home. (I used to do this when I had working AC. Makes a huge diference.)<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||loafer87gt||05-09-2000||12:22 PM||||I just put a couple of Bounce fabric softener sheets under my car seats. It gives the car a nice fresh smell.||||reg||1
